{#- Task call (task layer) user message — decision-first flow.

     Slot 7: the last per-turn call body, issued only after the decision
     call returned CONTINUE (renamed from `task_call.j2` 2026-09-07). See
     `prompts/README.md` for the assembled order.

     Rendered when ``ExperimentConfig.use_split_forfeit_layer=True`` as
     the SECOND of the two sequential LLM calls per turn, and only after
     the decision call returned CONTINUE (2026-09-04 reorder). Its job:

       - Let the agent analyse the task stimulus and commit to a RULE
         hypothesis + ACTION, exactly as in the single-call path but
         without the forfeit menu.

     The response-format block mirrors ``unified_turn_message.j2`` for
     RULE + ACTION only; CHOICE / REASON / STAKE never appear here — the
     continue/forfeit decision is already made, so the task call carries
     no forfeit vocabulary at all.

     Task-supplied response format (2026-09-01): a task module may expose
     ``get_response_format_override()`` returning a non-empty string. When
     it does, this template renders THAT block instead of the RULE +
     ACTION one, and suppresses the ACCEPT-only sentinel. This exists for
     task types whose answer is free-form rather than an action pick (the
     external-benchmark modules: Omni-MATH / Hi-ToM / GPQA), which return
     an empty ``available_actions`` list for a reason that has nothing to
     do with NullTask's "ACCEPT is the only valid response" semantics.
     Without the override those tasks were told both that ACCEPT was the
     only valid response and that they must emit ``ANSWER:``.

     The override is strictly additive: with ``response_format_override``
     absent or falsy, this template renders the standard RULE + ACTION
     block (pinned by ``tests/unit/test_task_call_template.py``).

     2026-09-10, prompt revision v2 (supervisor voice). No "===" marker;
     "LABEL: sentence" instead. The two lead sentences ("You may now
     analyze the puzzle and choose your action." / "... the problem and
     produce your answer.") collapse to "Give your answer." and the
     response-format lead to "ANSWER FORMAT: exactly two lines, in this
     order." (audit L5). Two evaluator words go with them (audit E2):
     "analyze the puzzle" named the genre every round, and the free-form
     RULE slot said "hidden rule" where the task rules say "the rule".
     The placeholder note now matches what the hint actually shows --
     ``___`` blanks, not ``<placeholder>`` (audit A4).

     Variables:
       user_body                : composed task stimulus + history (already
                                  trimmed by UnifiedTurnManager — no further
                                  wrapping).
       available_actions        : list[str]; empty → NullTask ACCEPT-only
                                  sentinel.
       rule_template_hint       : str|None; difficulty-aware RULE slot template
                                  (Phase L). None → free-form fallback.
       response_format_override : str|None; task-supplied response-format
                                  block replacing RULE + ACTION.
-#}
{%- if user_body -%}
{{ user_body }}

{% endif -%}
{%- if response_format_override -%}
Give your answer.
ANSWER FORMAT:
{{ response_format_override }}
{%- else -%}
{%- if not available_actions -%}
(This is a risk-only turn; the ACCEPT action is the only valid task response.)

{% endif -%}
Give your answer.
ANSWER FORMAT: exactly two lines, in this order.
{% if rule_template_hint %}RULE: {{ rule_template_hint }}
(Fill in every blank with a concrete value. Your ACTION must follow from your RULE.)
{% else %}RULE: <one-line best hypothesis of the rule; write "no rule" for null tasks>
{% endif %}ACTION: {% if available_actions %}<one of: {{ available_actions | join(", ") }}>{% else %}ACCEPT{% endif %}{% endif %}
